(3070399, 429494, 28742, '<td valign="top">Most Excellent! Congrats, Nerd! :)</td>', 'Most Excellent! Congrats, Nerd! :)', '2006-11-29 01:28:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(3070407, 429991, 4767, '<td valign="top">Nice wheels, Becky!  Feels a lot like 1955 to me. I do think seams were still ''happening'' about then.  I''d just noticed women''s legs and the seams made great leading lines... see - I was a dirty old man before my voice changed!</td>', 'Nice wheels, Becky!  Feels a lot like 1955 to me. I do think seams were still ''happening'' about then.  I''d just noticed women''s legs and the seams made great leading lines... see - I was a dirty old man before my voice changed!', '2006-11-29 01:29:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(3070443, 429946, 2382, '<td valign="top">Thank you ALL for the great comments!  I am so pleased with the scoring on this, my third competition.  I put more thought into this one than the previous two and I guess it helped.  Growing up in the 50''s/60''s I was always facinated with UFO''s and when this challenge came out I immediately thought of the famous McMinnville siting that occurred the year I was born.  I didn''t have time to try to find a closer match to the orig site but had fun looking for an old building that i could use.  I had a small metal lid to a sauce pan which I carried with me for several days so i could toss it up and shoot it if/when I found the right spot.  I located this shed during my lunch break one day...set up my tripod and started tossing and clicking.  I shot about 20 exposures of which 3 had the "UFO" up in the air.  I kept looking around to see if anyone was around but luckily I think i got away with doing this unseen.  It was great fun!  I was going to post a picture of my UFO in hand here for fun but I''m in Hawaii on vacation right now :-) so it will have to wait.  Again, thank you all for the votes and comments!</td>', 'Thank you ALL for the great comments!  I am so pleased with the scoring on this, my third competition.  I put more thought into this one than the previous two and I guess it helped.  Growing up in the 50''s/60''s I was always facinated with UFO''s and when this challenge came out I immediately thought of the famous McMinnville siting that occurred the year I was born.  I didn''t have time to try to find a closer match to the orig site but had fun looking for an old building that i could use.  I had a small metal lid to a sauce pan which I carried with me for several days so i could toss it up and shoot it if/when I found the right spot.  I located this shed during my lunch break one day...set up my tripod and started tossing and clicking.  I shot about 20 exposures of which 3 had the "UFO" up in the air.  I kept looking around to see if anyone was around but luckily I think i got away with doing this unseen.  It was great fun!  I was going to post a picture of my UFO in hand here for fun but I''m in Hawaii on vacation right now :-) so it will have to wait.  Again, thank you all for the votes and comments!', '2006-11-29 01:40:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(3070461, 430428, 53147, '<td valign="top">Go Team Qart, err, Untouchables!</td>', 'Go Team Qart, err, Untouchables!', '2006-11-29 01:48:18.000000', NULL, 0),
